#!/usr/bin/env etcs

# THE CANVAS DEMO: PaintProvider drawing through RenderProvider onto the page.
#
# Self-contained on purpose. The OS-side equivalents split the frame edge and
# the pointer edge into their own detachable scripts (RenderProvider's
# render_frames.etcs, PaintProvider's paint_pointer.etcs), and each of those
# would have to be mounted at its own URL for the browser to open it. Both are
# one `->` statement, so stating them here costs a line each and removes two
# mounts from the serve script.
#
# Nothing in this file is browser-specific. The same statements run on the OS
# side; what differs is which concrete Surface the contract selected
# (Contract_RenderProvider.h), and that is invisible from here.

spawn RenderProvider::Instance gpu
gpu.Create()

spawn WindowProvider::Window main
main.Create(1024, 768, ETCS Paint)

# A typed CHILD of the window, because Surface::Create walks getParent() for the
# window it draws into -- the parent link IS that binding.
main.spawn(RenderProvider::Surface view)
view.Create(@gpu)
view.Clear(0.13, 0.13, 0.15, 1.0)

# Two layers: paper underneath, ink on top. Both are CPU rasters (Pixels_), and
# the browser surface composites them with the same Blit the device backend uses.
spawn PaintProvider::PaintLayer paper
paper.Create(1024, 768)
paper.Clear(1.0, 1.0, 1.0, 1.0)

spawn PaintProvider::PaintLayer ink
ink.Create(1024, 768)
ink.Clear(0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0)

spawn PaintProvider::PaintDocument doc
doc.Create(1024, 768, browser)
doc.AddLayer(@paper)
doc.AddLayer(@ink)
doc.SetActiveLayer(@ink)

spawn PaintProvider::PaintTool brush
brush.SetRadius(6.0)
brush.SetColor(0.10, 0.10, 0.12, 1.0)

spawn PaintProvider::PaintSurface canvas
canvas.Create(@view)
canvas.AttachDocument(@doc)
canvas.Render()

spawn PaintProvider::PaintInput input
input.Create(@doc, @brush, @canvas)
input.SetBrush(6.0, 0.10, 0.10, 0.12, 1.0)

# ── the three pumps ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# AN EDGE BLOCKS THE THREAD THAT STATES IT, so only the LAST one can be stated
# here. The first two are detached, and they are the OS side's own scripts read
# from where the OS side keeps them -- the browser page stages them at these
# same relative paths (modules.json), so these two lines are the same lines
# paint_surface.etcs has.
#
# Nothing draws without the first. A Surface is RETAINED: Clear/Blit build a
# composition and something has to present it, so with no frame pump the window
# comes up, strokes accumulate into the layer, and the canvas stays blank --
# which reads as "painting is broken" rather than "nobody asked for a frame".
detach RenderProvider/scripts/render_frames.etcs view=view

# Positions on their own thread, presses on this one: the two channels are
# independent by construction (ontology/InputSource.h), so a press never queues
# behind a burst of pointer movement.
detach paint_pointer.etcs window=main input=input

# The press channel, and the OS message pump with it. Holds this thread until
# the window closes -- which in the browser is a detached worker, so the page
# stays live underneath it.
main.ProduceEvents() -> input.ConsumeInput()
